    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Lament"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Afterward Job opened his mouth and cursed the day of his birth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And Job said,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“May the day on which I was to be born perish,",
          "As well as the night which said, ‘A boy is conceived.’"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“May that day be darkness;",
          "May God above not care for it,",
          "Nor light shine on it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“May darkness and black gloom claim it;",
          "May a cloud settle on it;",
          "May the blackness of the day terrify it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“As for that night, may darkness seize it;",
          "May it not rejoice among the days of the year;",
          "May it not come into the number of the months."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Behold, may that night be barren;",
          "May no joyful shout enter it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“May those curse it who curse the day,",
          "Who are prepared to disturb Leviathan."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“May the stars of its twilight be darkened;",
          "May it wait for light but have none,",
          "And may it not see the breaking dawn;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Because it did not shut the opening of my mother’s womb,",
          "Or hide trouble from my eyes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶“Why did I not die at birth,",
          "Come out of the womb and pass away?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Why were the knees there in front of me,",
          "And why the breasts, that I would nurse?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“For now I would have lain down and been quiet;",
          "I would have slept then, I would have been at rest,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "With kings and counselors of the earth,",
          "Who rebuilt ruins for themselves;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Or with rulers who had gold,",
          "Who were filling their houses with silver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Or like a miscarriage which is hidden, I would not exist,",
          "As infants that never saw light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“There the wicked cease from raging,",
          "And there the weary are at rest."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“The prisoners are at ease together;",
          "They do not hear the voice of the taskmaster."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“The small and the great are there,",
          "And the slave is free from his master."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶“Why is light given to one burdened with grief,",
          "And life to the bitter of soul,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who long for death, but there is none,",
          "And dig for it more than for hidden treasures;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who are filled with jubilation,",
          "And rejoice when they find the grave?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Why is light given to a man whose way is hidden,",
          "And whom God has shut off?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“For my groaning comes at the sight of my food,",
          "And my cries pour out like water."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“For what I fear comes upon me,",
          "And what I dread encounters me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“I am not at ease, nor am I quiet,",
          "And I am not at rest, but turmoil comes.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
